--- 2.4 THE MISSING PREMISE, REGISTERED (the virial's NEW physics input)
    the EL contains:  the well's shape (C ln r), the constraints (M, E), the
    Boltzmann identification beta = 1/sigma^2.  It does NOT contain:
      (i)   T = (3/2) M_T sigma^2            -- kinematic energy of the fluid;
      (ii)  W_self = -G M_T^2/r_break        -- self-gravity of the phantom;
      (iii) W_bar = -M_b C ln(r_break/r_b)   -- coupling to the baryon well;
      (iv)  2T + W_self + W_bar = 3 P_s V    -- the mechanical balance that
            ties the dispersion to the potential depth (G091, sympy-exact).
    (i)-(iv) are DYNAMICS: they fix sigma^2 = C/2 (or, equivalently, the
    phantom slope gamma = 2) from the energy bookkeeping of a confined,
    self-gravitating isothermal fluid.  The entropy functional cannot produce
    them because counting microstates at fixed (M, E) presumes E -- and the
    splitting of E into kinetic vs potential -- as data of the problem.

================================================================================================
PART 3 -- VERDICTS
================================================================================================

  V1 THE DERIVATION ATTEMPT DOES NOT CLOSE (naive direction): the EL of the max-entropy problem at the fixed well yields the family rho = A r^(-C/sigma^2) -- one maximizer per temperature, all solving the EL to machine precision (0.25-2x C/2 tested) -- and the stationarity of the maximum (dS = 0 at fixed M, E) selects the profile for a GIVEN sigma^2, not a value of sigma^2: at every equilibrium (0.5, 1, 2 x C/2 tested) the identification dS/dE = 1/sigma^2 holds at that equilibrium's OWN temperature -- the multiplier IS the inverse temperature purely as a consistency, selecting no temperature -- and at fixed shape dS/dsigma^2 = -(3/2)/sigma^2 < 0 (the negative-signature of the self-gravitating microcanonical sphere; the counter-slope of the EL family dS/dE = +1/sigma^2 exists per equilibrium, both directions carry no extremum in sigma^2).  The phantom rho = A/r^2 is the maximizer AT sigma^2 = C/2 and at no other temperature -- the virial temperature is a PREMISE of the phantom, not an output of the EL.  The statistics converts the temperature into the profile; it does not generate the virial.

  V2 THE LEAN-READY THEOREM: THE REDUCED STATISTICAL VIRIAL -- let the max-entropy state at the fixed baryon well Phi = C ln r, C = sqrt(G M_b a0), obey the EL identity gamma = C/sigma^2 (the energy multiplier IS the inverse temperature, beta = 1/sigma^2, G084).  Then sigma^2 = C/gamma (an exact inversion), and at the phantom closure gamma = 2 (rho = A/r^2, the equilibrium's isothermal profile -- Lean-certified M01/G227/C07/EQUILIBRIUM_THEORY, measured p = 2.000 at the MW interior, G072/G188): sigma^2 = C/2 = (1/2) sqrt(G M_b a0) -- the spine's rung E2 closes as pure algebra {max-entropy EL identity} x {certified phantom slope}.  The candidate Lean statements compile exit 0, zero sorry, axioms {propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound}: statistical_virial (the abstract closure), statistical_virial_instantiated (at C = sqrt(G M_b a0)), el_identity_inverse (the inversion), el_family_free and phantom_half_closure (the boundary and its symbolic instance).  THE FULL CLAIM 'max entropy generates the virial with no external mechanical input' is NOT a theorem; its missing premise is registered: the kinetic-vs-potential balance 2T + W_self + W_bar = 3 P_s V (G091) -- the virial's NEW physics input, which fixes gamma = 2 (or sigma^2 directly) -- with the G091 closed chain (C1, virial_rung4) remaining the alternative mechanical Lean route to the same number.

  V3 THE HONEST STATEMENT -- THE STATISTICAL VIRIAL EXISTS IN REDUCED FORM, AND THE VIRIAL'S BALANCE IS A GENUINELY SEPARATE PHYSICS INPUT: the max-entropy functional at the fixed well derives the profile from the temperature (rho = A r^(-C/sigma^2), EL-exact at every sigma^2) and -- inverted -- the temperature from the profile (sigma^2 = C/gamma), so that with the phantom slope gamma = 2, E2 = sigma^2 = sqrt(G M_b a0)/2 lands as a theorem of the max-entropy state (Lean-ready, compiled).  What the statistics does NOT contain, stated without garnish: the kinetic-vs-potential balance -- the equality 2T + W = 3 P_s V that a bound, self-gravitating, confined fluid must satisfy -- is dynamics, not counting: S[rho] knows the well's shape but not why the fluid hovers against it, so no entropy maximization can select sigma^2 = C/2 among the family of temperatures.  The rung's honest anatomy: E2 = {EL identity (statistical, certified-able: G214 C2)} x {phantom slope gamma = 2 (equilibrium datum, certified: M01/G227)} -> sigma^2 = C/2, with the virial's mechanical content (G091, C1) as the dynamical premise fixing the slope -- the derivation EL -> phantom -> VIRIAL does not close; the derivation {EL identity} x {phantom} -> sigma^2 = C/2 does, exactly, and that is the statistical virial's honest, Lean-able content.

